---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, OPERATOR_EMAIL, OPERATOR_NAME } from '../data/site';

const GOOGLE_POLICY_URL = 'https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy';
const GOOGLE_PERMISSIONS_URL = 'https://myaccount.google.com/permissions';
const CNIL_URL = 'https://www.cnil.fr/';
// Matches the 180-day purge in the server (internal/jobs).
const INACTIVITY_DAYS = 180;
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy of the hosted Google Contacts MCP service: what it stores about you, what it never stores (your contacts), and how to erase your data."
  path="/privacy"
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
>
  <h2>Who runs this service</h2>
  <p>
    This service is operated by {OPERATOR_NAME}, an individual, who is responsible for your data. Contact:{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR_EMAIL}`}>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What the service does</h2>
  <p>
    It lets an AI assistant you connect, such as Claude or ChatGPT, read and update your Google Contacts. Every tool call
    reads or writes Google directly; nothing about your contacts is kept.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your Google account id and your e-mail address, with the dates your account was created and last used. The e-mail
      address is stored in clear, so the operator can find your account when you ask to be disconnected.
    </li>
    <li>Your Google refresh and access tokens, encrypted.</li>
    <li>Hashes of the tokens this server issues to your assistant, with their expiry. Never the tokens themselves.</li>
    <li>The assistants (OAuth clients) registered with this server.</li>
    <li>Sign-ins in progress: they expire after 10 minutes and are deleted within the hour.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is never stored</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your contacts: names, e-mail addresses, phone numbers, notes or any other field.</li>
    <li>The tool inputs and outputs exchanged with your assistant.</li>
    <li>Any token in clear.</li>
    <li>Contact data, tool arguments or results in logs at the default log level.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    At the default log level, each tool call writes one log line: the tool name, an internal user id, the duration and
    the status. At that level, arguments and results are not logged, and tokens never are.
  </p>

  <h2>How your data is protected</h2>
  <p>Your contacts and your Google tokens are sensitive data. These measures protect them:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>In transit.</strong> Every connection to this service uses HTTPS (TLS), and so do the calls this service makes
      to Google.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>At rest.</strong> Your Google tokens are encrypted with AES-256-GCM before they reach the database, and each
      one is bound to the user it belongs to. The encryption keys are not stored in the database, and they can be rotated.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contacts are not stored.</strong> Contact data passes through memory during one tool call. It is never
      written to the database or to disk.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tokens issued to your assistant</strong> are opaque, and only their hashes are stored. Access tokens last 1
      hour. Refresh tokens rotate on every use, and reusing an old one revokes the whole token family.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Least privilege.</strong> Sign-in uses OAuth 2.1 with PKCE (S256), and tokens are bound to this service's
      endpoint. Tools accept only contact and group identifiers, so a tool call cannot reach any other Google resource.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Access control.</strong> Access to the server, its database and its encryption keys is limited to the
      operator and the hosting provider.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Abuse limits.</strong> Per-user rate limits apply to reads and writes. Logs never contain tokens, secrets or
      Google responses.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Incidents.</strong> If a breach affects your data, the operator revokes the affected Google grants, informs
      you by e-mail, and notifies the CNIL when the law requires it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use of Google data</h2>
  <p>
    This service requests three Google scopes: <code>openid</code> and <code>email</code> identify your Google account,
    and <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/contacts</code> lets your assistant read and update your Google Contacts.
    It requests no other Google user data.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google data is used only to perform the actions your assistant requests. The results of those actions are returned to
    the assistant you connected, and handled by its provider under its own privacy policy. This service does not share
    them with anyone else, sell them, or use them for advertising or to train models.
  </p>
  <p>
    This service's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href={GOOGLE_POLICY_URL}
      >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
    >, including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The tokens issued to your assistant expire after 1 hour (access) and 180 days (refresh).</li>
    <li>
      An account unused for {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days is purged automatically, and its Google grant is revoked.
    </li>
    <li>
      An assistant registered with the server is deleted when it has not been used for {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days, or 24 hours
      after registering if it never signed anyone in.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to erase everything</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Ask the operator at <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR_EMAIL}`}>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</a> to disconnect you: your Google grant is
      revoked and every row about you is deleted from the live database.
    </li>
    <li>
      Revoke access yourself at <a href={GOOGLE_PERMISSIONS_URL}>myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Your data is deleted
      the next time you use the connector after revoking access at Google; if you never use it again, the automatic purge
      above removes it.
    </li>
    <li>Stop using it: accounts unused for {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days are purged.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The database lives on a persistent storage volume. Deleted data can remain in backups of that volume, if the operator
    or the hosting provider keeps any, until they expire under the backup retention; Google tokens stay encrypted there
    too.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis and recipients</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is processed only to provide the service you asked for: connecting your assistant to your Google Contacts.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is handled by Google, which hosts your contacts and may process data outside the European Union; by the assistant
    you connect; and by the hosting provider that stores this service's database.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of the data stored about you, in a portable format, or for its correction, restriction or deletion, and you can object to its processing, by e-mail. If you think your
    data is mishandled, you can complain to the CNIL, the French data protection authority, at{' '}
    <a href={CNIL_URL}>cnil.fr</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. It loads nothing from another site: even its fonts are served from
    the site itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes, the date at the top changes too. The conditions of use are in the <a href="/terms"
      >terms of service</a
    >.
  </p>
</Legal>
